hadiths[4]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1245","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim Al-Durqi and Ziyad bin Ayyub told us, saying: Hushaym told us, Khalid told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaqiq, He said: I asked Aisha about the voluntary prayer of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and she said: “He used to pray long nights standing, and long nights sitting. So when he recites while standing, he kneels and prostrates while standing, and if he recites while sitting, he kneels and prostrates while sitting.”"
"1246","Ahmad bin Abdah told us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Zaid, told us, on the authority of Badil, and Ayyub, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaqiq, on the authority of Aisha, She said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “used to pray for a long night, standing, so if he prayed standing, he bowed standing, and if he prayed sitting, he bowed sitting.”"
"1247","Muhammad bin Al-Ala bin Kurayb told us, Abu Khalid told us, Humaid told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaqiq, on the authority of Aisha, that He asked her about the prayer of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sitting, and she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “was praying a long night, standing up.” If he prayed sitting, he bowed sitting, and if he prayed standing, he bowed standing.” Abu Khaled said: I narrated it to Hisham bin Urwa, and he said: Humaid lied and Abdullah bin Shaqiq lied. My father told me, on the authority of Aisha, She said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, never prayed sitting until he entered the age, so he used to recite the surahs, and if there were verses left from them, he would stand up. So he recited them, then bowed, and this is what Abu Bakr said: The surahs. Abu Bakr said: Hisham ibn Urwa denied the information about Abdullah ibn Shaqiq, as it appears that he had a contradiction to his information from his father. On the authority of Aisha, and in my opinion it does not contradict his report. Because in Khalid’s narration, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaqiq, on the authority of Aisha: If he recites while standing, he kneels and prostrates while standing, and when he recites While he was sitting, he knelt and prostrated while he was sitting. Based on this wording, this news is not unlike the news of Urwa and Amra, on the authority of Aisha; Because this word that Khaled mentioned indicates that if he did all of the recitation while sitting, he would bow while sitting, and if all of the recitation was While reciting while standing, he kneeled while standing, and Abdullah bin Shaqiq did not mention the description of his prayer if some of the recitation was standing and some of it was sitting, but rather It was mentioned by Urwa, Abu Salamah, and Amra, on the authority of Aisha, if the recitation in both cases was some standing and some sitting, He mentioned that he used to kneel while standing when his recitation was in both cases, and he did not mention Urwa, Abu Salamah, or Umrah. How did the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, begin this prayer, in which he recites standing and sitting, and kneels while standing? Ibn Sirin mentioned, on the authority of Abd Allah bin Shaqiq, on the authority of Aisha, there is evidence that he used to open it while standing."
"1248","Sallam bin Junada told us, Waki` told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaqiq al-Uqaili, on the authority of Aisha said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “used to pray standing and sitting, so if he began the prayer standing, he would kneel standing, and if he began the prayer standing Sitting, he bowed while sitting.” Abu Bakr said: This narration explains all of these narrations. According to this narration, if he began the prayer standing, then sat and recited, he should He may stand and recite part of his recitation, then bow while standing. If he begins his prayer sitting, he will recite all of his recitation while sitting. Then he bowed while sitting, following the action of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace."
